    {
      "id": 228679,
      "name": "aramis",
      "username": "aramis",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/aramis/{size}/1871_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-09-21T10:10:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>While I'd love to see a broad licensing, I think the D&amp;D Community Content model is not a good one. Excessive percentages, lots of low quality content, no route to the FLGS, forfeiture of copyright rights. It's one thing to get a decent paycheck for a work for hire as a freelancer, it's another entirely to forfeit the IP for potentially trivial cash. Futher, the way the license is set up, it's very possible that they could pull a GW and go after fans' personal websites.<br>\n<br>\nI do think non-onerous licensing is a good thing, even with a fee... but most of the Community Content licenses have onerous provisions.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:03:14.463Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 3,
      "readers_count": 2,
      "score": 5.6,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 19427,
      "topic_slug": "will-there-be-a-place-for-community-content",
      "display_username": "aramis",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
